WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 1: Welcome to School.

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:10.540
In this first unit, your child learns the
words for things in the classroom, some colours,

3
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.780
and how to say their own name and age.

4
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.240
They meet the idea that school is a happy, welcoming place.

5
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.340
The goal is warm, confident first
steps in English — not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:27.220
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:34.500
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
common classroom objects (table, chair, book, pencil…).

8
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.520
you will also name and point to
colours (red, blue, green, yellow…).

9
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.440
you will also say “my name is ___.

10
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.140
i am ___ years old.

11
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.000
i like ___.”.

12
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.940
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:58.500
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
table, chair, whiteboard, ABC chart, clock, book.

14
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.360
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.840
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.260
The reading sequence includes Amal's
First Day and Talk about Welcome to School.

17
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:14.800
Read actively.

18
00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:20.080
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.300
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.120
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

21
00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:33.580
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: This is a ___.

22
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:41.500
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.320
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

24
00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:51.300
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.860
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.340
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.040
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.300
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.920
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.680
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
